# XSH uname()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The format of each member is implementation-defined, so only that each is
# a null-terminated string inside its array, and that the identifying ones
# are not empty, is checked. nodename is only required to be terminated.

assertion  XSH.uname.001
anchor     functions/uname.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/uname.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       uname() returns a non-negative value and fills the structure:
           sysname, nodename, release, version and machine are each
           null-terminated within their arrays, and sysname, release,
           version and machine are not empty.
test       t/001-fields.c

assertion  XSH.uname.002
anchor     functions/uname.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       Repeated calls, also from a child process, give the same sysname,
           release, version and machine.
test       t/002-stable.c
